 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on the disguises, never on a victim (none appears). Every case is a seizure announced by U.S. Customs and Border Protection (a settled fact); the hook states the seizure. Nobody accused is named or drawn: the Otay Mesa driver (29, turned over to Homeland Security Investigations, no charge reported) appears only as a typed label; no arrest was announced in the two Pharr cases and no driver appears. Officers are generic figures in plain dark navy work uniforms with no badge, patch, flag, agency name or insignia; no weapon shown or mentioned; no force shown. The K-9 is shown sitting calmly beside its handler (an alert), unharmed. Trucks, trailers, crates and berry flats carry no company name, logo or plate; the scanner image is a generic grey silhouette with our own typed boxes, not any real system's interface; the manifest is our own blank form with the single typed word WATERMELONS. The inspection table, the dock, the cargo lanes and the scan room are illustrations, not reported scenes. Every card is our own typed graphic; no dialogue or quotation card. Facts verified 2026-10-21.",
