 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Friday 16 August 2024, Otay Mesa Commercial Facility (San Diego, the port of entry with Tijuana): CBP officers seized more than $5 million worth of methamphetamine disguised and concealed within a shipment of watermelons. Narration: 'Smugglers dressed meth up as watermelons.' / '$5 million worth, ...' Headline 'FAKE WATERMELONS / FULL OF METH'. Label 'OTAY MESA, SAN DIEGO · AUG 2024'.",
   "sources": [
    "cbp",
    "hstoday",
    "apabc",
    "npr",
    "abc7news",
    "abc7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_weight",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The packages weighed 4,587 lb (2,080 kg) and were found among a real watermelon shipment (AP: 'among real watermelons'). Narration: '..., among real ones.' Counter 4,587 LB in the next shot.",
   "sources": [
    "apabc",
    "npr",
    "hstoday",
    "freshplaza",
    "mnd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_unload",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The 29-year-old driver's tractor-trailer was referred for additional examination at secondary inspection, where the watermelon shipment was offloaded for further examination (AP: 'unloaded for a detailed inspection'). No dog or imaging is mentioned in any extract, so none is claimed. Narration (gotcha): 'But officers unloaded the truck.'",
   "sources": [
    "apabc",
    "freshplaza",
    "hstoday",
    "npr"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_skins",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Officers found 1,220 packages wrapped in paper coloured to look like watermelon skins (CBP: 'disguised as watermelons within the shipment'); the contents tested as methamphetamine. Narration: '1,220 had paper skins.' Callout 'PAPER SKIN · METH', 'Among real melons (CBP)'.",
   "sources": [
    "apabc",
    "hstoday",
    "freshplaza",
    "abc7news",
    "pa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_stat",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "STATISTIC (counter 4,587 LB): the total weight CBP gave for the 1,220 packages. Counter '4,587 LB' with the label 'METH · 1,220 FAKE MELONS'.",
   "sources": [
    "hstoday",
    "apabc",
    "npr",
    "freshplaza"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_driver",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "CBP seized the drugs and the tractor-trailer; the driver, a 29-year-old man, was turned over to Homeland Security Investigations. He was not named and no charge was reported in the extracts. Label sub 'Driver, 29, turned over to HSI · not named' (the hook's location label). Never drawn.",
   "sources": [
    "hstoday",
    "apabc",
    "npr",
    "abc7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_leeks",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "22 August 2026, Pharr International Bridge cargo facility, Texas: CBP officers found suspected methamphetamine worth about $10.75 million (KRGV: $10.8 million) in a tractor-trailer from Reynosa, Mexico, whose shipment was declared as leeks. Narration: 'And that was not the biggest.' (editorial rehook, true: $10.75M > $5M) / 'Then leeks: nearly $11 million.' Label 'DECLARED: LEEKS · PHARR, TEXAS', 'Aug 2026 · about $10.75 million (CBP)'.",
   "sources": [
    "freightwaves",
    "foxrgv",
    "krgv",
    "trucker"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_leekcatch",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "At secondary inspection, non-intrusive inspection equipment showed anomalies in the trailer and a canine team alerted to narcotics; a physical search found 395 packages weighing 1,204.82 lb. CBP seized the drugs and the truck; HSI opened a criminal investigation; no arrest was announced and no driver named. Narration (gotcha): 'The scanner flagged it. So did the dog.' Label '395 PACKAGES · 1,204 LB', 'Scanner anomalies + a K-9 alert (CBP)'.",
   "sources": [
    "freightwaves",
    "krgv",
    "trucker",
    "foxrgv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_celery",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT: one week before the watermelons, on 9 August 2024, officers at the same Otay Mesa facility found 629.72 lb of methamphetamine (508 packages, about $755,000) in a celery shipment, after a K-9 alert. Card 'SAME PORT AS THE MELONS, / ONE WEEK EARLIER: / 629 LB OF METH IN CELERY'.",
   "sources": [
    "abccelery",
    "tosd",
    "10news"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_berries",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "23 March 2026, Pharr International Bridge cargo facility: a tractor-trailer from Reynosa carrying a shipment of blackberries held suspected methamphetamine with an estimated street value of $17,737,200 (HSToday headline: 'Meth Labelled as Blackberries'). Narration: 'The biggest? Blackberries.' / '$17 million inside.' Labels 'PHARR, TEXAS · MARCH 2026', '$17,737,200 · CBP'.",
   "sources": [
    "hstoday26",
    "fox7",
    "fox4",
    "freshplaza26",
    "producenews"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_scan",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Officers referred the truck to a secondary inspection dock, where they used non-intrusive scanning equipment to examine the fruit shipment, then extracted the packages. Narration (gotcha): 'One scan later: 862 packages found.' Label 'NON-INTRUSIVE SCAN, THEN A SEARCH'.",
   "sources": [
    "hstoday26",
    "fox7",
    "freshplaza26"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_862",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Officers extracted 862 packages of suspected methamphetamine weighing 1,984.16 lb (900 kg); CBP seized the drugs and the vehicle and HSI opened a criminal investigation; no arrest announced in the extracts. Label '862 PACKAGES · 1,984 LB · $17.7M'.",
   "sources": [
    "hstoday26",
    "fox7",
    "fox4",
    "freshplaza26"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_manifest",
   "type": "established",
